{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user provided a detailed stitch task (#5102) to implement display flags for `cmd/cat` in the go-unix-utils project. Specifically:\n   - Task R1: Implement srd006-cat R2.4 — `-E` flag to display `\n\n at end of each line\n   - Task R2: Implement srd006-cat R3.1 — `-T` flag to display TAB characters as `^I`\n   - Task R3: Implement srd006-cat R3.2 — `-v` flag to show non-printing characters using `^` and `M-` notation\n   - Task R4: Implement srd006-cat R3.3 — combined flag shorthands (`-A`, `-e`, `-t`) per SRD definitions\n   \n   Acceptance criteria: AC1 (go build succeeds), AC2 (go vet passes), AC3 (-E appends $ to lines), AC4 (-v displays non-printing correctly).\n   \n   The task is part of a cobbler-scaffold code generation pipeline. Git is managed externally — NO git commands should be run.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU cat non-printing character display: caret notation (`^X`) for control chars, `M-` prefix for high-bit chars\n   - Character ranges: 0x00-0x1F → `^X`, 0x7F → `^?`, 0x80-0x9F → `M-^X`, 0xA0-0xFE → `M-X`, 0xFF → `M-^?`\n   - Tab (0x09) and newline (0x0A) are exempted from `-v` transformation per R4.2\n   - Order of operations per R4.9: squeeze blanks → non-printing display (-v/-T) → end-of-line marker (-E) → line number (-n/-b)\n   - Combined flag shorthands: `-A` = `-v -E -T`, `-e` = `-v -E`, `-t` = `-v -T`\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` against GNU reference binary `gcat`\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines (E8 constitution rule)\n   - File size limit: 500 lines (E9 constitution rule)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd006-cat.yaml`\n     - Read to understand full requirements. Key sections: R4.1-R4.9 define non-printing display behavior. R4.1 defines exact caret/M- notation. R4.2 exempts tab and newline from -v. R4.3 defines -E ($ before newline). R4.4 defines -T (tab as ^I). R4.5-R4.7 define combined shorthands. R4.9 defines transformation order.\n   \n   - `cmd/cat/main.go` (MODIFIED — complete rewrite via Write tool)\n     - This is the only file to create/modify per the task spec.\n     - Added three new flag variables: `flagV`, `flagE`, `flagT`\n     - Extracted flag application into `applyFlag(c rune)` function to keep parseFlags under 40 lines\n     - Updated `catFile` fast-path check to include new flags: `!flagV && !flagE && !flagT`\n     - Added `writeTransformed(w *bufio.Writer, line []byte)` — processes bytes: newlines get `\n\n prefix if flagE, tabs become `^I` if flagT, other bytes go through `writeVisible` if flagV\n     - Added `writeVisible(w *bufio.Writer, b byte)` — implements M- and caret notation: bytes >= 128 get \"M-\" prefix and 128 subtracted, then bytes < 32 get `^` + (b+64), byte 127 gets `^?`, others pass through\n     - Full written file:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     // cmd/cat implements srd006-cat: file concatenation with line numbering,\n     // blank squeezing, and non-printing display.\n     package main\n     \n     import (\n     \t\"bufio\"\n     \t\"errors\"\n     \t\"fmt\"\n     \t\"io\"\n     \t\"os\"\n     \n     \t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     var (\n     \tflagN bool\n     \tflagB bool\n     \tflagS bool\n     \tflagV bool\n     \tflagE bool\n     \tflagT bool\n     )\n     \n     func main() {\n     \tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n     \targs := parseFlags(os.Args[1:])\n     \tif len(args) == 0 {\n     \t\targs = []string{\"-\"}\n     \t}\n     \texitCode := 0\n     \tlineNum := 1\n     \tprevBlank := false\n     \tfor _, name := range args {\n     \t\tvar err error\n     \t\tlineNum, prevBlank, err = catFile(name, lineNum, prevBlank)\n     \t\tif err != nil {\n     \t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"cat: %s\\n\", formatErr(err))\n     \t\t\texitCode = 1\n     \t\t}\n     \t}\n     \tif exitCode != 0 {\n     \t\tos.Exit(exitCode)\n     \t}\n     }\n     \n     func parseFlags(args []string) []string {\n     \tvar files []string\n     \tendOfFlags := false\n     \tfor _, arg := range args {\n     \t\tif endOfFlags || arg == \"\" || arg == \"-\" || arg[0] != '-' {\n     \t\t\tfiles = append(files, arg)\n     \t\t\tcontinue\n     \t\t}\n     \t\tif arg == \"--\" {\n     \t\t\tendOfFlags = true\n     \t\t\tcontinue\n     \t\t}\n     \t\tfor _, c := range arg[1:] {\n     \t\t\tapplyFlag(c)\n     \t\t}\n     \t}\n     \treturn files\n     }\n     \n     func applyFlag(c rune) {\n     \tswitch c {\n     \tcase 'n':\n     \t\tflagN = true\n     \tcase 'b':\n     \t\tflagB = true\n     \tcase 's':\n     \t\tflagS = true\n     \tcase 'v':\n     \t\tflagV = true\n     \tcase 'E':\n     \t\tflagE = true\n     \tcase 'T':\n     \t\tflagT = true\n     \tcase 'A':\n     \t\tflagV = true\n     \t\tflagE = true\n     \t\tflagT = true\n     \tcase 'e':\n     \t\tflagV = true\n     \t\tflagE = true\n     \tcase 't':\n     \t\tflagV = true\n     \t\tflagT = true\n     \tcase 'u':\n     \t\t// R4.8: accepted but ignored\n     \tdefault:\n     \t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"cat: invalid option -- '%c'\\n\", c)\n     \t\tos.Exit(1)\n     \t}\n     }\n     \n     func catFile(name string, lineNum int, prevBlank bool) (int, bool, error) {\n     \tvar r io.Reader\n     \tif name == \"-\" {\n     \t\tr = os.Stdin\n     \t} else {\n     \t\tf, err := os.Open(name)\n     \t\tif err != nil {\n     \t\t\treturn lineNum, prevBlank, err\n     \t\t}\n     \t\tdefer f.Close()\n     \t\tr = f\n     \t}\n     \tif !flagN && !flagB && !flagS && !flagV && !flagE && !flagT {\n     \t\t_, err := io.Copy(os.Stdout, r)\n     \t\treturn lineNum, prevBlank, err\n     \t}\n     \treturn catTransform(r, lineNum, prevBlank)\n     }\n     \n     func catTransform(r io.Reader, lineNum int, prevBlank bool) (int, bool, error) {\n     \tbr := bufio.NewReader(r)\n     \tw := bufio.NewWriter(os.Stdout)\n     \tfor {\n     \t\tline, err := br.ReadBytes('\\n')\n     \t\tif len(line) > 0 {\n     \t\t\tlineNum, prevBlank = writeLine(w, line, lineNum, prevBlank)\n     \t\t}\n     \t\tif err != nil {\n     \t\t\tif err == io.EOF {\n     \t\t\t\tbreak\n     \t\t\t}\n     \t\t\treturn lineNum, prevBlank, err\n     \t\t}\n     \t}\n     \tif ferr := w.Flush(); ferr != nil {\n     \t\treturn lineNum, prevBlank, ferr\n     \t}\n     \treturn lineNum, prevBlank, nil\n     }\n     \n     func writeLine(w *bufio.Writer, line []byte, lineNum int, prevBlank bool) (int, bool) {\n     \tisBlank := len(line) == 1 && line[0] == '\\n'\n     \tif flagS && isBlank && prevBlank {\n     \t\treturn lineNum, true\n     \t}\n     \tif (flagN || flagB) && !(flagB && isBlank) {\n     \t\tfmt.Fprintf(w, \"%6d\\t\", lineNum)\n     \t\tlineNum++\n     \t}\n     \tif flagV || flagE || flagT {\n     \t\twriteTransformed(w, line)\n     \t} else {\n     \t\tw.Write(line)\n     \t}\n     \treturn lineNum, isBlank\n     }\n     \n     func writeTransformed(w *bufio.Writer, line []byte) {\n     \tfor _, b := range line {\n     \t\tif b == '\\n' {\n     \t\t\tif flagE {\n     \t\t\t\tw.WriteByte(')\n     \t\t\t}\n     \t\t\tw.WriteByte('\\n')\n     \t\t\tcontinue\n     \t\t}\n     \t\tif b == '\\t' {\n     \t\t\tif flagT {\n     \t\t\t\tw.WriteString(\"^I\")\n     \t\t\t} else {\n     \t\t\t\tw.WriteByte('\\t')\n     \t\t\t}\n     \t\t\tcontinue\n     \t\t}\n     \t\tif flagV {\n     \t\t\twriteVisible(w, b)\n     \t\t\tcontinue\n     \t\t}\n     \t\tw.WriteByte(b)\n     \t}\n     }\n     \n     func writeVisible(w *bufio.Writer, b byte) {\n     \tif b >= 128 {\n     \t\tw.WriteString(\"M-\")\n     \t\tb -= 128\n     \t}\n     \tif b < 32 {\n     \t\tw.WriteByte('^')\n     \t\tw.WriteByte(b + 64)\n     \t} else if b == 127 {\n     \t\tw.WriteByte('^')\n     \t\tw.WriteByte('?')\n     \t} else {\n     \t\tw.WriteByte(b)\n     \t}\n     }\n     \n     func formatErr(err error) string {\n     \tvar pe *os.PathError\n     \tif errors.As(err, &pe) {\n     \t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s: %s\", pe.Path, pe.Err)\n     \t}\n     \treturn err.Error()\n     }\n     ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. The file was written but build/vet/test verification has NOT been run yet.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Designed the byte-by-byte transformation to correctly handle the interaction between -v, -E, and -T flags\n   - Tab (0x09) and newline (0x0A) are checked BEFORE calling writeVisible to respect R4.2 exemption, while their high-bit equivalents (0x89, 0x8A) are correctly transformed via the M- prefix path\n   - Extracted `applyFlag()` from `parseFlags()` to keep both functions under the 40-line limit (E8 constitution rule)\n   - The fast path in catFile was updated to check all six flags\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The massive task description providing the stitch task #5102 with all project context, SRDs, architecture, requirements, constraints, execution constitution, and the specific task to implement display flags (-E, -T, -v, -A, -e, -t) in cmd/cat/main.go.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Run `go build -o bin/cat ./cmd/cat/` to verify AC1 (compilation succeeds)\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/cat/` to verify AC2 (no warnings)\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/cat/... -count=1` to verify differential tests pass (if test file exists)\n   - The task constraints say: \"Complete all code changes before running go build or go test. Do not compile incrementally after each small edit.\"\n\n8. Current Work:\n   The file `cmd/cat/main.go` has been fully written with all required display flag functionality (-E, -T, -v, -A, -e, -t). The Write tool confirmed success. The next step is to verify the acceptanc